            <ArticleTitle>Unusual presentation of cyathostomiasis in an adult Thoroughbred mare.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>1221-1223</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>A recently purchased 16-year-old Thoroughbred mare with a history of recurrent colic and low body weight, also had lameness in 3 limbs, pain at the sacro-iliac joint, and increased corneal opacity of the right eye. Response to supportive therapy was poor and euthanasia was elected. A postmortem examination and histopathology confirmed cyathostomiasis within the large colon and cecum and chronic anterior uveitis of the right eye.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
